# A two-way bus through a 74HC245: one set of wires A1..A4 that carries data both ways.
# DIR high (0..8 ms): the counter U1 drives the A side through the 3-state buffer U2 (enabled by NDIR low), and the 245 copies A
# to the B side (B1..B4 follow the count). DIR low (8..16 ms): U2 lets go of the A side, the 245 turns round and drives A from the
# B side, where four resistors set the value 5 (B1 and B3 high), like DIP switches. The digital view shows A[1..4] and B[1..4].
# Build: cargo run -p cli -- docs/examples/bus_transceiver.ccad, then put "analysis": {"tran_stop": "16m", "tran_step": "10u", ...}
# into the .schjson (the end time the sample opens with)
new
add V 5 as=V1
add V 0 as=VCK
value VCK "PULSE(0 5 0 1u 1u 0.5m 1m)"
add V 0 as=VDIR
value VDIR "PULSE(5 0 8m 1u 1u 8m 16m)"
add 74HC161 as=U1
add 74HC244 as=U2
add 74HC04 as=U3
add 74HC245 as=U4
add R 10k as=R1
add R 10k as=R2
add R 10k as=R3
add R 10k as=R4
net VCC V1.+ U1.VCC U2.VCC U3.VCC U4.VCC U1.CLR U1.LOAD U1.ENP U1.ENT U2.2OE R1.1 R3.1
net GND V1.- VCK.- VDIR.- U1.GND U2.GND U3.GND U4.GND U1.A U1.B U1.C U1.D U2.2A1 U2.2A2 U2.2A3 U2.2A4 U3.2A U3.3A U3.4A U3.5A U3.6A U4.OE U4.A5 U4.A6 U4.A7 U4.A8 U4.B5 U4.B6 U4.B7 U4.B8 R2.1 R4.1
net CLK VCK.+ U1.CLK
net DIR VDIR.+ U3.1A U4.DIR
net NDIR U3.1Y U2.1OE
net QA U1.QA U2.1A1
net QB U1.QB U2.1A2
net QC U1.QC U2.1A3
net QD U1.QD U2.1A4
net A1 U2.1Y1 U4.A1
net A2 U2.1Y2 U4.A2
net A3 U2.1Y3 U4.A3
net A4 U2.1Y4 U4.A4
net B1 U4.B1 R1.2
net B2 U4.B2 R2.2
net B3 U4.B3 R3.2
net B4 U4.B4 R4.2
nc U1.RCO U2.2Y1 U2.2Y2 U2.2Y3 U2.2Y4 U3.2Y U3.3Y U3.4Y U3.5Y U3.6Y
erc
tran 16m 10u probe=V(DIR),V(A1),V(A2),V(A3),V(A4),V(B1),V(B2),V(B3),V(B4)
save docs/examples/bus_transceiver.schjson
